Subject: [PATCH 67/67] feat(threads): each GET /threads row says the owner's
 role (frontend 06:30Z item 3)

The frontend's 06:30Z list (Misho, the new design), item 3: the list's role
filter and the header pill need the owner's role in each conversation.
Nothing marked a mediator, so the app drew no role there rather than guess.

Each row now carries role:
- mediator: an introduction request came to them, in the request's own
  thread or in a conversation it was written into;
- addressee: someone's goal asked them;
- initiator: their own goal or their own introduction request;
- null: a plain conversation with no work in it.
It is read in the same list query. Checked read-only on live.

DONE WHEN: a bridge's request thread reads mediator, an asked person's
thread addressee, a goal thread initiator, a plain chat null.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
